; ============================================================ ; and V is cleared  which is NOT the same as being
                                                               ; spent
                                                               ; X really is gone: the conveyor consumed it a byte at
                                                               ; a time and the halvings took each byte to nought; V
                                                               ; is not; shifting right in this field REDUCES  so bits
                                                               ; are fed back in at the top and after a hundred and
                                                               ; twenty eight shifts V holds a residue rather than
                                                               ; nought; A caller that copied a fresh value in over it
                                                               ; would be adding to that residue  so this block clears
                                                               ; it and says so below  rather than leaving every
                                                               ; caller to remember; aes/ghash128's exit contract is
                                                               ; what caught it
